---
import Account from "../../layouts/Account.astro";
import DashboardDrawing from "../../components/DashboardDrawing.astro";
import "../../styles/cli-studio.css";
---
<Account title="Connect" titleAccent="your CLI." section="tokens">
  <div class="cli-studio">
    <aside class="cli-web-note"><span class="cli-note-icon" aria-hidden="true">↗</span><div><strong>Publishing here on the website?</strong><p>You don’t need a token. CLI access is only for working from your terminal or automation.</p></div><a href="/publish">Open Publish <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></aside>
    <nav class="cli-journey" aria-label="CLI setup and access"><a href="#token-create"><span aria-hidden="true">01</span><strong>Create a token</strong><small>Choose its access</small></a><a href="#cli-setup"><span aria-hidden="true">02</span><strong>Connect your terminal</strong><small>Set two variables</small></a><a href="#cli-run"><span aria-hidden="true">03</span><strong>Try a command</strong><small>Search or submit</small></a><a href="#cli-token-list-title"><span aria-hidden="true">04</span><strong>Manage access</strong><small>Review or revoke</small></a></nav>
    <div class="cli-setup-grid">
      <form id="token-create" class="cli-create" aria-labelledby="token-create-title" novalidate>
        <header class="cli-section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">01 / YOUR ACCESS</p><h2 id="token-create-title">Create a token</h2><p>A token lets the CLI act with the access you choose.</p></div><span class="cli-expiry-badge">Valid for 30 days</span></header>
        <div class="form-field"><label for="token-label">Give it a name</label><input id="token-label" required maxlength="100" autocomplete="off" placeholder="For example, my laptop" aria-describedby="token-label-help" /><p id="token-label-help" class="field-help">A reminder of where you’ll use it. This is not the secret.</p></div>
        <div class="form-field"><label for="token-scope">What should it be able to do?</label><select id="token-scope" aria-describedby="token-scope-help"><option value="publish">Submit extension packages</option><option value="read">Read the private registry</option></select><p id="token-scope-help" class="field-help">Submit packages for one publisher. Scanning and review still apply.</p></div>
        <div class="form-field" id="token-namespace-field"><label for="token-namespace">Publisher namespace</label><select id="token-namespace" required aria-describedby="token-namespace-help"></select><p id="token-namespace-help" class="field-help">Choose a publisher you belong to.</p><p id="token-namespace-empty" hidden class="cli-inline-note">You’ll need a publisher namespace for submission access. <a href="/account/namespaces">Create or join a namespace ↗</a></p></div>
        <footer class="cli-create-footer"><button class="button" id="token-create-button" type="submit" disabled>Create token <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button><p>You’ll see the secret once. Save it before leaving.</p></footer>
        <p id="token-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" class="cli-feedback" tabindex="-1">Loading your access…</p>
      </form>
      <aside class="cli-access-guide" aria-labelledby="cli-access-guide-title"><DashboardDrawing section="tokens" /><p class="eyebrow">SMALL KEY. SPECIFIC ACCESS.</p><h2 id="cli-access-guide-title">Only what<br /><em class="editorial-accent">your tools need.</em></h2><dl><div><dt>Submission access</dt><dd>Send packages for one publisher namespace. It doesn’t publish them instantly.</dd></div><div><dt>Read access</dt><dd>Browse the private catalog and download signed packages. No namespace needed.</dd></div></dl><p class="cli-boundary">Neither option can manage your team, approve submissions or bypass review.</p></aside>
    </div>
    <section id="token-secret-section" hidden class="cli-secret" aria-labelledby="token-secret-title"><p class="eyebrow">TOKEN CREATED / SAVE IT NOW</p><h2 id="token-secret-title" tabindex="-1">Your key to the next step.</h2><p>This secret is shown once. Store it securely and use it in step 2. Keep it out of source code, URLs, logs and screenshots.</p><label for="token-secret">Your new token</label><input id="token-secret" readonly autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" /><div class="actions"><button class="button" id="token-copy" type="button">Copy token</button><button class="button secondary" id="token-hide" type="button">I’ve saved it · hide secret</button></div><p id="token-secret-feedback" class="cli-feedback" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><p id="token-expiry"></p></section>
    <section class="cli-terminal" id="cli-setup" aria-labelledby="cli-setup-title"><header class="cli-section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / CONNECT YOUR TERMINAL</p><h2 id="cli-setup-title">A quick setup. Then you’re in.</h2><p>Already have <code>tabsext</code>? Set the registry and your token in the terminal where you’ll use it.</p></div><a href="/developers">Get the CLI ↗</a></header><div class="cli-command-block"><div><span>Terminal setup</span><button type="button" id="token-setup-copy" class="button secondary">Copy setup</button></div><pre><code id="token-instructions"></code></pre></div><p id="token-setup-feedback" class="cli-feedback" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><p class="field-help">Replace <code>&lt;your-token&gt;</code> with your saved secret. The copy button copies placeholders, never your secret. Use a temporary terminal session and avoid saving the secret in shell history.</p><details class="cli-command-help"><summary>Prefer to enter the token without showing it?</summary><p>In bash, use <code>read -rs TABS_EXCHANGE_TOKEN; export TABS_EXCHANGE_TOKEN</code>. In zsh, use <code>read -rs 'TABS_EXCHANGE_TOKEN?Token: '; export TABS_EXCHANGE_TOKEN</code>. Paste the secret at the prompt; it won’t appear on screen.</p></details></section>
    <section class="cli-run" id="cli-run" aria-labelledby="cli-run-title"><header class="cli-section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">03 / YOUR FIRST COMMAND</p><h2 id="cli-run-title">Take it for a spin.</h2><p>Use the command that matches your token’s access.</p></div></header><div class="cli-command-grid"><article><h3>Search the catalog</h3><p>Works with read or submission access.</p><pre><code>tabsext search --registry "$TABS_EXCHANGE_ORIGIN"</code></pre></article><article><h3>Submit a package</h3><p>Needs submission access for the package’s publisher.</p><pre><code>tabsext publish my-tool.tabsext --registry "$TABS_EXCHANGE_ORIGIN" --tabs-version '&lt;your-tabs-version&gt;'</code></pre><p>Replace the filename and Tabs version. <a href="/account/extensions">Follow the review in Submissions ↗</a></p></article></div><p class="cli-cleanup">Finished? Run <code>unset TABS_EXCHANGE_TOKEN</code> to remove the token from this terminal’s environment.</p></section>
    <section class="cli-token-ledger" aria-labelledby="cli-token-list-title"><header class="cli-section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">MANAGE YOUR ACCESS</p><h2 id="cli-token-list-title">Your tokens <span id="token-count"></span></h2><p>Keep track of what’s connected. Revoke access when a tool no longer needs it.</p></div><button class="button secondary" id="token-refresh" type="button">Refresh list</button></header><p id="token-list-feedback" class="cli-feedback" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><ul id="token-list" aria-label="Your access tokens"></ul></section>
  </div>
</Account>
<script>import "../../scripts/tokens";</script>
